hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17747","Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Ziyad informed us, from Fatik ibn Fadala, from Ayman ibn Khuraym who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood addressing and said: O people, false testimony equals associating with Allah, three times. Then he recited: So avoid the filth of idols and avoid false speech."
"18208","Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Fatik ibn Fadalah from Ayman ibn Khuraym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to address and said: O people, false testimony has been made equal to associating partners with Allah, three times, then he said: So avoid the impurity of idols and avoid false speech."
